            <ArticleTitle>[Diabolically intense axillary-scapular pain in a colleague].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2107-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a middle-aged patient, in whom a rare subluxation of the costotransversal joint caused a severe axillary pain. Diagnosis was not achieved by imaging studies or electroneuromyography, but instead simply by palpation. A good treatment outcome was obtained by manipulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
